Golden Path linters — concept and Solisol CLI rule schema
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The "linter-to-agent" concept in MemKeys — surfacing a project's guardrails to
agents as a first-class part of memory retrieval (the `applicable_linters`
block returned alongside facts on memory_fetch / memory_search) — originates
with:

    Jessica Andersson (Solisol)
    https://github.com/Solisol

The MemKeys-native linter rule shape (see docs/golden-path-linters.md and
docs/adr/ADR-0004-linter-data-model.md) is designed to round-trip with the
Solisol CLI rule schema. Specifically, the fact `body` of a `linter` fact is a
superset-aligned structure: the `match` block (including `match.solisol_rule`),
the `severity` / `message` / `fix_hint` fields, and verbatim preservation of
unknown rule keys exist so that a Solisol ruleset can be represented in MemKeys
without loss.

This is a body-shape alignment and acknowledgement, not a code dependency on
Solisol. No Solisol source code is vendored into this repository. If a formal
bidirectional converter between the Solisol CLI rule format and the MemKeys
linter body is added in the future, it will be coordinated with Jessica
Andersson and credited at that time.
